title: Example - TABLE with multiline cells
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Table

Live demo for cells that hold multiple paragraphs. The trick: use the inline `TH`/`TD` markers for one-line cells (no `<p>` wrap), and the block `BLOCKTH`/`BLOCKTD` markers only where you actually need paragraph breaks. Block cells terminate at `||` so blank lines can live inside them.

!! Source

```
TABLE
ROW
TH Power
TH Batman
TH Flash
--
ROW
TH Skill
BLOCKTD Plays chess. Reads books.

Practices martial arts.
||
BLOCKTD Super speed. Vibrates through walls.

Time travel as a side effect.
||
--
---
```

!! Rendered

TABLE ROW
TH Power
TH Batman
TH Flash
--
ROW
TH Skill
BLOCKTD Plays chess. Reads books.

Practices martial arts.
||
BLOCKTD Super speed. Vibrates through walls.

Time travel as a side effect.
||
--
---

Header row uses inline `TH` (one line each, no `<p>` wrap). The data row mixes an inline `TH` row-label with two block-mode `BLOCKTD` cells, each holding two paragraphs separated by a blank line and terminated by `||`.

Terminator pyramid: `||` ends each `BLOCKTH`/`BLOCKTD`; `--` ends each `ROW`; `---` ends the `TABLE`.

See [[Customize a Table with Multiline Content]] for the marker schema and the pragma-form alternative.

